p('Priority improvements','Heading2');p('1. Collect all labels at a common documented snapshot and, ideally, predict a fixed horizon such as 30-day views. Store immutable source evidence and distinguish upload time, extraction time and measurement time.<br/>2. Record channel audience, paid media spend and placement, region, language and platform. These may explain reach more directly than creative descriptions.<br/>3. Manually review campaign groups, source annotations and missing/weak evidence. Evaluate leave-brand-out and time-based splits to probe harder generalization.<br/>4. Expand the sample and repeat grouped splits; report campaign-level bootstrap intervals. Test random/no-edge graphs, graph k and feature-block scaling with matched model capacity.<br/>5. Use bilingual sentence representations or better Chinese segmentation fitted without response information. Validate extracted creative settings against the actual video.')
p('Limitations','Heading2');p('This is a curated collection of advertising references, not a random sample of all videos. Collection windows differ by package and timestamp availability is nonuniform. Creative labels are source-produced interpretations and can be redundant or inconsistent. A single outer holdout and modest sample size limit generalization. Optimization can exploit model error or mismatch between the categorical settings and the unchanged text. No new upload experiment, traffic uplift measurement or causal identification was performed.')
